{"imdb_tconst": "tt9916362", "imdb_user": "RosanaBotafogo", "imdb_user_review_topic": "And They flew...\\n", "imdb_user_review": "It's a film that hurts the soul, for we are sure it was even worse than the film, the reality, I stopped a few times, by the feeling of discomfort and discomfort caused by some scenes, the poetic and hopeful ending... The film troops inquisitors, and we see blind and disoriented faith, when even the youngest priest and friend of the girls, who finally see them as witches... And They flew...", "imdb_user_review_date": "19 June 2021", "imdb_user_rating": 9, "imdb_n_helpful_vote": 2, "imdb_t_vote": 2, "url": "https://www.imdb.com/title/tt9916362/reviews", "spider": "imdb_user_review", "date": "20/08/2021"}
{"imdb_tconst": "tt9916362", "imdb_user": "bsant54", "imdb_user_review_topic": "17th C (1609) Mood Lighting &amp; Spanish Caliente\\n", "imdb_user_review": "One thing about the Spanish, muy caliente, to say the least.The girls were awesome. When they realized what was going to happen to them well they went out with a dance and some good food provided by idiot inquisitors wanting to see a real Devil witch ceremony...which tells you how gullible men are (and I am a guy). Add in some magic mushrooms and it made for a great MUY CALIENTE ending.The inquisitor was good in this. He played along with the one girl's story about the Devil Sabbath ceremony. She weaved an irresistible sexy, lust filled tale and near the end, she had him hook, line and sinker (he swallowed it all, well played gradual lust by him).No seagulls soared. But the girls did in dance a celebration of womanhood so much so, the Abbess disrobed to show her femininity and in song celebrated the girls. And, the inquisitor had a magic mushroom and made the point of the girls that he was the Devil in this.The daytime lighting was moody, dream like and the nighttime was crystal clear, razor sharp even by candle or woodfire.A fun, fun show. Predictable ending but for a moment on the moon lit cliff...I was hoping for the Devil and NOT the inquisitor.", "imdb_user_review_date": "13 March 2021", "imdb_user_rating": 8, "imdb_n_helpful_vote": 8, "imdb_t_vote": 15, "url": "https://www.imdb.com/title/tt9916362/reviews", "spider": "imdb_user_review", "date": "20/08/2021"}
{"imdb_tconst": "tt9916362", "imdb_user": "najeebspencershasan", "imdb_user_review_topic": "Great Acting and Directing\\n", "imdb_user_review": "Although this genre has been explored before, what I enjoyed thoroughly was acting and the direction of this movie. Kudos to the director and the actors were not only good but awesome! Although watching at home on Netflix, I felt and the climax is a must watch ! Of course it's horrible how the women were treated during those invasions but what stands out is the perfect execution.", "imdb_user_review_date": "12 March 2021", "imdb_user_rating": 10, "imdb_n_helpful_vote": 10, "imdb_t_vote": 20, "url": "https://www.imdb.com/title/tt9916362/reviews", "spider": "imdb_user_review", "date": "20/08/2021"}
{"imdb_tconst": "tt9916362", "imdb_user": "alexxluonto", "imdb_user_review_topic": "Tens across the board!\\n", "imdb_user_review": "Beautiful cinematography, amazing acting and a strong storyline that leaves a mark on you. Hauntingly realistic peak to the history books made for modern audiences with themes that resonates.\\nThis movie not only subvert the generalized theme of witches in cinema but breathes new air to the subject while bringing about the themes of oppression and obsession amongst others. Not a single second in this movie lets you down.Will be adding to my favorites and can't wait to watch it again soon.", "imdb_user_review_date": "19 March 2021", "imdb_user_rating": 10, "imdb_n_helpful_vote": 5, "imdb_t_vote": 9, "url": "https://www.imdb.com/title/tt9916362/reviews", "spider": "imdb_user_review", "date": "20/08/2021"}
{"imdb_tconst": "tt9916362", "imdb_user": "Pairic", "imdb_user_review_topic": "In search of the Black Sabbath\\n", "imdb_user_review": "Coven Of Sisters: Set in the Basque country in 1609, very much in the mould of Witchfinder General but far darker. A Witchfinder along with his scribe, interrogator (torturer) and platoon of soldiers is progressing along the coast, seeking out Witches and Heretics. So far they have burned seventy seven women at the stake along with three Parish Priests who were found wanting. The Witchfinder Rostegul (Alex Brendermuhl) wants to observe an actual black Sabbath, in the next village six teenage girls are arrested, having been denounced as Witches, he wants to force them to reveal their Demonic secrets. but of course they have none. The brightest among them, Ana (Amala Aberasturi) tries to trick the Inquisitor, pretending to chant the Black Mass when is she in fact singing Basque folk songs, the other girls join in. Their intent is to delay their executions until the men of the village return from sea who will then fight off the Witchfinder's men. There are disturbing scenes of torture but more is implied than actually shown. The real horror is psychological as the girls as the girls are thrown into a dark cell, not knowing what they are accused of. Rostegul twists their words to imply guilt, even what they haven't said is used to incriminate them. But Anna along with some older women use the Inquisitor's fanaticism against him, keeping his interest and postponing her fate as Scheherazade did. A savage film which you'll remember and mull over longer after the end credits have rolled. Directed by Pablo Aguero, Screenplay by Pablo Aguero and Katell Guillou. On Netflix. 8/10.", "imdb_user_review_date": "17 March 2021", "imdb_user_rating": 8, "url": "https://www.imdb.com/title/tt9916362/reviews", "spider": "imdb_user_review", "date": "20/08/2021"}
{"imdb_tconst": "tt9916362", "imdb_user": "billcr12", "imdb_user_review_topic": "Witches Beware\\n", "imdb_user_review": "Here is a film based on the Spanish Inquisition in the 1600's. A judge arrives at a small fishing village and with his cohorts interrogates young woman with accusations of witchcraft. The nuns at my Catholic school failed to mention this unsavory part of our history. Religion in all forms can be used in dangerous ways. The women here are tortured to the point of confessing to relations with the devil. The atmosphere is historically accurate and the actors are good. It will not restore your faith in humanity or religion, but it is a worthwhile viewing.", "imdb_user_review_date": "22 April 2021", "imdb_user_rating": 6, "imdb_n_helpful_vote": 2, "imdb_t_vote": 3, "url": "https://www.imdb.com/title/tt9916362/reviews", "spider": "imdb_user_review", "date": "20/08/2021"}
{"imdb_tconst": "tt9916362", "imdb_user": "toz451", "imdb_user_review_topic": "Wow\\n", "imdb_user_review": "Such a well done movie! So interesting. Really takes you along on this incredible, sensual, and sad journey. Not for those who want the typical Hollywood gore. There's plenty of those out there for you. This is something else.", "imdb_user_review_date": "13 April 2021", "imdb_user_rating": 8, "imdb_n_helpful_vote": 2, "imdb_t_vote": 3, "url": "https://www.imdb.com/title/tt9916362/reviews", "spider": "imdb_user_review", "date": "20/08/2021"}
{"imdb_tconst": "tt9916362", "imdb_user": "kosmasp", "imdb_user_review_topic": "Sisterhood of (f)lying witches\\n", "imdb_user_review": "Obviously I'm taking liberty with that \\\"sisterhood of travelling pants\\\" book and movie thing ... you know trying to be funny. But me going down that road does not mean this is a comedy. Far from it, this is as serious as they come ... and reveal themselves.And while some may be aware of the history of witches and especially movies, I do think this has a somewhat original take on it. Not that there are many twists and turns that you can't predict. But it does evolve in a way and has character flaws in it ... that really are quite something to behold.It was \\\"easy\\\" to be accused of being a witch back in the day ... though the reasoning behind it might have varied - scorned or rejected male, a woman that might be too self empowered and supersticion in general. The movie balances the occult and the craziness in a wonderful manner and sets a tone that will haunt you a long time after it is over ... or at least it can have that affect.", "imdb_user_review_date": "31 March 2021", "imdb_user_rating": 8, "url": "https://www.imdb.com/title/tt9916362/reviews", "spider": "imdb_user_review", "date": "20/08/2021"}
