{"imdb_tconst": "tt9916362", "imdb_user": "asiereu-1", "imdb_user_review_topic": "Not about Spanish Inquisition, but based in historical events.\\n", "imdb_user_review": "Film based on historical events that appears to be largely unknown as it is accused of being historically inaccurate. Well, it is based on the Labourd witchcraft trials in 1609 carried out by Pierre de Lancre or Pierre de Rosteguy, a French judge who took advantage of the absence of fishermen in the ports to prosecute the alleged witchcraft. Later He wrote three books on witchcraft, and many of the myths about witches and their rites are detailed.", "imdb_user_review_date": "17 August 2021", "imdb_user_rating": 10, "imdb_n_helpful_vote": 0, "imdb_t_vote": 0, "url": "https://www.imdb.com/title/tt9916362/reviews", "spider": "imdb_user_review", "date": "20/08/2021"}
