{"imdb_tconst": "tt9916362", "imdb_user": "packmanproductions", "imdb_user_review_topic": "Like A Bad High School Play\\n", "imdb_user_review": "So the religious idiots of 17th century Basque Country decided to round up women who live near the woods and try them as witches. Of course, they're all guilty in the minds of these sorcerer believing half-wits which leads to burning the poor girls at the stake. Between the poor acting and the nonexistent script this is a big time waster. Most of the non-action that takes place in this movie occurs in a dungeon. If you're looking for some important message to derive from this low budget bore-fest it would be to not waste your time.", "imdb_user_review_date": "18 March 2021", "imdb_user_rating": 1, "imdb_n_helpful_vote": 7, "imdb_t_vote": 36, "url": "https://www.imdb.com/title/tt9916362/reviews", "spider": "imdb_user_review", "date": "20/08/2021"}
{"imdb_tconst": "tt9916362", "imdb_user": "teocrito", "imdb_user_review_topic": "Terrible movie. Not worth anyone's time\\n", "imdb_user_review": "I couldn't finish it. It was desperately slow and dull. I thought it would show how the Inquisition worked in the XVII century. I'm a history teacher and I was thinking to watch it with my students but it's terribly written and historically inaccurate.The girls accused of witchcraft seem like they were taken from this contemporary time to that century. They act and think like girls from the XX century.The inquisitors are stupid beyond repair, what they do it doesn't make any sense. None. And is because the writers don't know a thing about history. They just took elements from an average exorcist movie, clich\\u00e9s from the Spanish Inquisition, some postmodernist feminism here and there and mix it up together with no quality or style.Avoid like the plague.", "imdb_user_review_date": "1 June 2021", "imdb_user_rating": 1, "imdb_n_helpful_vote": 3, "imdb_t_vote": 11, "url": "https://www.imdb.com/title/tt9916362/reviews", "spider": "imdb_user_review", "date": "20/08/2021"}
